 |\n                                                 | (Delegates via IVehicleRepository)\n                                                 v\n                       +---------------------------------------------------+\n                       |                IVehicleRepository                 |\n                       +---------------------------------------------------+\n                               /                                   \\\n                              /                                     \\\n                             v                                       v\n             +-------------------------------+       +-------------------------------+\n             |   InMemoryVehicleRepository   |       |    SupabaseVehicleRepository  |\n             |   (Using SEED_VEHICLES)       |       |    (Future Backend API / DB)  |\n             +-------------------------------+       +-------------------------------+\n```\n\n1. **Strict Type Safety**: All 22 requested attributes (including `id`, `brand`, `model`, `variant`, `year`, `price`, `currency`, `fuelType`, `transmission`, `bodyType`, `horsepower`, `torque`, `mileage`, `engine`, `seating`, `safetyRating`, `bootSpace`, `dimensions`, `features`, `image`, `gallery`, `description`) plus performance telemetry (`zeroToSixty`, `topSpeed`) are defined on `Vehicle`.\n2. **Repository Pattern (Pluggable Backend)**:\n   - `IVehicleRepository` contract guarantees UI components never contain database queries or hardcoded arrays.\n   - `InMemoryVehicleRepository` executes fast multi-token search, multi-criteria filtering, and spec matrix comparisons over `SEED_VEHICLES`.\n   - When connecting to PostgreSQL/Supabase, a `SupabaseVehicleRepository` can be swapped in via `VehicleService.setRepository(...)` with **zero changes** required in UI components.\n3. **Seed Data Composition (23 Vehicles)**:\n   - **Hatchbacks**: *Volkswagen Golf R, Honda Civic Type R, Hyundai Ioniq 5 N*\n   - **Sedans**: *BMW M3 Competition, Mercedes-Benz S580 4MATIC, Audi RS7 Performance, Tesla Model S Plaid*\n   - **SUVs**: *Porsche Cayenne Turbo GT, Range Rover SV, Lamborghini Urus Performante, Rivian R1S Quad-Motor, Aston Martin DBX707*\n   - **Luxury Cars**: *Rolls-Royce Spectre, Bentley Continental GT Speed, Mercedes-Maybach S680*\n   - **Electric Vehicles**: *Porsche Taycan Turbo S, Lucid Air Sapphire, Audi e-tron GT RS, Rimac Nevera*\n   - **Performance / Supercars**: *Porsche 911 GT3 RS, Ferrari 296 GTB, McLaren 750S, Chevrolet Corvette Z06*\n\n---\n\n### 3. Verification\n- **TypeScript Typecheck (`npx tsc --noEmit`)**: **0 errors**\n- **Next.js Production Build (`npm run build`)**: **Compiled successfully with all static pages optimized**\n\nI have stopped here as instructed before proceeding to the next feature."}
{"step_index":302,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-01T12:01:54Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nNow move to STEP 7: build the Explore Cars experience for AutoMind AI.\r\n\r\nThe vehicle data architecture from STEP 6 is complete and verified.\r\n\r\nIMPORTANT:\r\n\r\n* Use the existing VehicleService and repository architecture.\r\n* Do NOT create a new car data structure.\r\n* Do NOT hard-code vehicle arrays inside React components.\r\n* Do NOT modify the existing homepage hero unnecessarily.\r\n* Do NOT implement Gemini or ML yet.\r\n\r\nCreate the main vehicle exploration route:\r\n\r\n/explore\r\n\r\nIf the current application uses a different existing route such as /cars, use the existing convention consistently, but make sure the homepage \"Explore Cars\" CTA points to the final exploration route.\r\n\r\nPAGE STRUCTURE:\r\n\r\n1. Page Header\r\n\r\nTitle:\r\n\"EXPLORE CARS\"\r\n\r\nSubtitle:\r\n\"Discover machines engineered for every kind of drive.\"\r\n\r\nAdd a subtle automotive-themed animated background treatment consistent with the homepage.\r\n\r\n2. Search\r\n\r\nCreate a prominent search bar:\r\n\r\nPlaceholder:\r\n\"Search by brand, model or vehicle...\"\r\n\r\nSearch should use VehicleService.searchCars().\r\n\r\nSearch should work across relevant vehicle fields such as:\r\n\r\n* brand\r\n* model\r\n* variant\r\n* body type\r\n* fuel type\r\n\r\n3. Filters\r\n\r\nCreate a responsive filter sidebar/drawer.\r\n\r\nFilters:\r\n\r\nBrand\r\nBody Type\r\nFuel Type\r\nTransmission\r\nPrice Range\r\nYear Range\r\n\r\nUse VehicleService.filterCars().\r\n\r\nOn desktop:\r\n\r\n* filters can appear in a sidebar.\r\n\r\nOn mobile:\r\n\r\n* filters should open in a drawer/modal.\r\n\r\n4. Sorting\r\n\r\nAdd a sorting control with:\r\n\r\n* Featured\r\n* Price: Low to High\r\n* Price: High to Low\r\n* Newest\r\n* Highest Horsepower\r\n* Best Mileage\r\n\r\nUse the existing VehicleService.sortCars() method.\r\n\r\n5. Vehicle Grid\r\n\r\nDisplay the vehicles using reusable VehicleCard components.\r\n\r\nEach card should show:\r\n\r\n* vehicle image\r\n* brand\r\n* model\r\n* variant\r\n* price\r\n* fuel type\r\n* transmission\r\n* horsepower\r\n* mileage\r\n* body type\r\n\r\nAdd:\r\n\r\n* View Details button\r\n* Compare button\r\n* Favorite button\r\n\r\n6. Vehicle Card Design\r\n\r\nMake the cards feel premium and automotive.\r\n\r\nUse:\r\n\r\n* rounded but sophisticated surfaces\r\n* subtle borders\r\n* image hover zoom\r\n* smooth Framer Motion entrance\r\n* hover elevation\r\n* subtle glow\r\n* clean typography\r\n\r\nDo NOT overuse animations.\r\n\r\n7. Result Count\r\n\r\nShow something like:\r\n\r\n\"23 VEHICLES\"\r\n\r\nUpdate the count dynamically when filters/search are applied.\r\n\r\n8. Empty State\r\n\r\nIf no vehicle matches:\r\n\r\n\"NO MACHINES FOUND\"\r\n\r\nAdd:\r\n\"Try adjusting your filters or search.\"\r\n\r\nAdd a \"Clear Filters\" button.\r\n\r\n9. Loading State\r\n\r\nCreate a polished loading skeleton for vehicle cards.\r\n\r\n10. Error State\r\n\r\nCreate a reusable error state.\r\n\r\n11. Responsive Design\r\n\r\nThe page must work properly on:\r\n\r\n* desktop\r\n* laptop\r\n* tablet\r\n* mobile\r\n\r\n12. Vehicle Details Route\r\n\r\nCreate a dynamic route:\r\n\r\n/explore/[id]\r\n\r\nClicking \"View Details\" should open the correct vehicle.\r\n\r\nThe details page should initially show:\r\n\r\n* large vehicle image\r\n* brand\r\n* model\r\n* variant\r\n* price\r\n* year\r\n* fuel\r\n* transmission\r\n* horsepower\r\n* torque\r\n* mileage\r\n* engine\r\n* seating\r\n* safety rating\r\n* boot space\r\n* features\r\n* description\r\n\r\nAlso include buttons for:\r\n\r\n\"Compare\"\r\n\"Ask AI About This Car\"\r\n\"Predict Its Value\"\r\n\r\nThe last two buttons can be placeholders for now. Do not implement Gemini or ML yet.\r\n\r\n13. Data Architecture\r\n\r\nAll vehicle information must come through:\r\n\r\nVehicleService\r\n→ repository\r\n→ vehicle data\r\n\r\nDo not directly import SEED_VEHICLES into page components unless the existing architecture specifically requires it.\r\n\r\n14. Accessibility\r\n\r\nEnsure:\r\n\r\n* buttons have accessible labels\r\n* form controls have labels\r\n* keyboard navigation works\r\n* sufficient contrast\r\n* images have alt text\r\n\r\n15. Performance\r\n\r\nAvoid unnecessary client-side rendering.\r\n\r\nUse server components where appropriate and client components only where interactivity requires them.\r\n\r\nAfter implementation:\r\n\r\n1. Run npx tsc --noEmit\r\n2. Run npm run build\r\n3. Fix all errors\r\n4. Verify all routes\r\n5. Verify search\r\n6. Verify filters\r\n7. Verify sorting\r\n8. Verify dynamic vehicle details\r\n9. Verify mobile layout\r\n\r\nThen STOP.\r\n\r\nReport:\r\n\r\n* files created\r\n* files modified\r\n* routes created\r\n* features implemented\r\n* TypeScript result\r\n* production build result\r\n* any remaining issues\r\n\r\nDo not proceed to STEP 8.\r\n\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-09-01T17:31:54+05:30.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
